// Regression for PR #399: a destructuring assignment binds `trans` to the
// constant return of a multi-return function, and mesh() placement folds that
// destructured constant to position the assets. Before the fix `trans` could
// not be folded (buildScope skipped multi-name assignments and there was no
// way to evaluate one return of a multi-return function), so the mesh map
// unroll silently dropped — producing zero asset nodes. Mirrors the
// manifold.branch() / positions = map(... rotateXY(trans, ...) ...) shape.
branch() {
  field = length(p) - 5;   // p-dependent return (stand-in SDF)
  trans = [60, 0, -40];    // constant return
  return field, trans;
}

castPart, trans = branch();

// A map over the destructured constant produces the placement list; each
// element must fold so the mesh map can unroll to one asset per position.
positions = map((ang) { return trans + [ang * 10, 0, 0]; }, [0, 1]);

return meshUnion(map(
  (value, index) { return mesh(0, value); },
  positions
));
